    "chunk_text": "supervisory framework for Virtual Asset Service Providers including a survey to identify existing Virtual Asset Service Providers operating in Sri Lanka. (iv) Appointing a Ministerial-level Subcommittee on Virtual Asset Service Providers established under the policy guidance of the AML/CFT National Coordinating Committee to oversee the establishment of a prudential regulatory framework for Virtual Assets and Virtual Asset Service Providers. (v) Draft a concept paper and road map for\n\nregard: (a) Preparing a regulatory approach to prudentially register and regulate Virtual Assets and Virtual Asset Service Providers. One of the Bills we are presenting today relates to Virtual Asset Service Providers. (b) Preparing an Anti-Money Laundering and\n\nCountering the Financing of Terrorism regulatory approach via the Amendments to the Financial Transactions Reporting Act. For the AML/CFT supervisory purposes, the FIU has started a phased-out approach to implement Financial Action Task Force Recommendations for Virtual Asset Service Providers. In line with this approach, the Financial Transactions Reporting Act, No. 6 of 2006 has already been amended. The proposed AML/CFT framework for Virtual Asset Service Providers, as implemented by the FIU with the approval of the Governing Board of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka, is structured according to the following timeline: \u2022 July, 2025 to December, 2025 - Identification\n\nof Virtual Asset Service Providers and implementation of the awareness and outreach initiatives. \u2022 January, 2026 to June, 2026 - Integration of\n\nVirtual Asset Service Providers into the AML/CFT framework, with the initiation of supervision and monitoring. \u2022 July, 2026 to December, 2026 - Identification\n\nof a prudential regulator for Virtual Asset Service Providers. \u2022 Four Subcommittee meetings were already\n\nheld to discuss the way forward and for implementing the phased Action Plan.\n\n429 430\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 