    "md5": "a79a3d2706f9ec8a19a18e022cab843a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1973,
    "chunk_text": "4. Delimitation of Provincial Council Constituencies - prepare a report on utilizing the Noel Tittawella Commision\u2019s electorates (160) as an alternative to the constituencies prepared under the 50:50 First-Past-the-Post to Proportional Representation system.\n\nName Designation\n\nheld Duration\n\n1. Dr. K. Thavalingam Chairman / Member\n\nFrom November 2015 to December, 2020\n\n3. Prof. H.S. Hasbullah Member From November 2015 to August, 2018\n\n4. Mr. A.M. Nahiya (Following\n\nthe demise of Prof. Hasbullah) Member From March 2019 to December, 2020\n\n5. Mr. Mahinda Deshapriya Chairman / Member\n\nFrom January 2021 to May, 2023\n\n6. Mr. J.R.W. Dissanayake Member From January 2021 to May, 2023\n\n7. Mr. P.H.G. Premasiri Member From January 2021 to May, 2023\n\n8. Dr. K. Thavalingam Chairman / Member\n\nFrom June 2023 to December, 2025\n\n9. Dr. (Ms.) A.D. Bandaranaike Member From June 2023 to December, 2025\n\n10. Mr. M.I. Ameer Member From June 2023 to December, 2025\n\n5. Study the Gazette Notifications published regarding the boundaries of administrative units.\n\n6. Publish articles in newspapers and\n\nmagazines.\n\n7. Compile and publish six limited-edition\n\nbooks related to delimitation.\n\n8. Develop a website for the Delimitation\n\nCommission.\n\n9. Maintain a collection of information and\n\ndocuments related to delimitation.\n\n10. Review and evaluate the recommendations made by the Delimitation Committees of 2012 and 2021.\n\n(iv) Salaries and Allowances\n\nPayment of salaries and allowances from 2015 to 2025 amounts to Rs. 48,611,865.00.\n\nProvision of Facilities\n\nTransport facilities have been provided to the Chairman.\n\nPayment of Office Rent\n\nThe Office of the Commission is functioning at the Surveyor General\u2019s Office building free of rent. No expenditure has been incurred for this purpose.\n\n(b) (i) \u2022 Permanent cadre at the Delimitation\n\nCommission - 08 \u2022 Acting cadre - 02\n\n(ii)\n\n(iii) The amount expended on employees' salaries from 2015 to 2025 is Rs. 58,782,533.00."
