    "chunk_size_bytes": 1269,
    "chunk_text": "Sir, I refute some of the points that the Hon. Members from the Opposition put forward saying that this Government is not working towards the development of tourism in the Northern region, including Jaffna. Actually, we have identified Jaffna as an area which had suffered with less investments, poor infrastructure for development projects and due to lack of entrepreneurial motivation for the local crowd. That happened in the past, but, as I said, immediately after the present Government took office, we asked all the provinces to develop strategic plans for tourism development. The Northern Province has now completed that task and based on that, we keep on investing.\n\n709 710\n\n\u0db4\u0daf\u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dda\u0dca\u0dca \u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dc0\u0dca\u200d\n\nreport will be submitted to the Government very soon and, based on that, we will start our work on domestic aviation. At the moment, there are a few private companies working on air transportation. But, as the Government, our involvement would mainly be based on that report because we are not facilitating just one place, but we need to work on a long-term strategic plan, relating to which we are waiting for the World Bank\u2019s report. So, I would like to mention that our Government is continuously working on developing domestic aviation."
