    "chunk_text": "report will be submitted to the Government very soon and, based on that, we will start our work on domestic aviation. At the moment, there are a few private companies working on air transportation. But, as the Government, our involvement would mainly be based on that report because we are not facilitating just one place, but we need to work on a long-term strategic plan, relating to which we are waiting for the World Bank\u2019s report. So, I would like to mention that our Government is continuously working on developing domestic aviation.\n\nIn terms of human capital development, we launched a project with the Department of Samurdhi Development to attract the unemployed youth to the tourism industry. Under that project, the Sri Lanka Institute of Tourism and Hotel Management is actively running the Hotel Operations Multitasker Course relating to the hospitality sector. Actually, six months back, we launched that programme and 82 youth from the Jaffna District and 64 from Kilinochchi have completed this course, and we have directed them for employment. Currently, there are 105 students from the Jaffna District and 80 students from the Kilinochchi District following the course, whom we will direct very soon to the tourism and hospitality sector for employment as well. For the upcoming batch in August, we are planning to recruit 100 from the Jaffna District and another 100 from the Kilinochchi District. So, in terms of human capital development also, we have prioritized the Northern Province, including the Jaffna District. We believe that we would be able to get many youth, who had dealt with weapons for decades, employed in growing sectors like tourism. At the same time, we have secured a land from Jaffna to establish a full-fledged hotel school so that we could run comprehensively all such programmes at that place. And, we would look for investment, particularly from the diaspora in the coming years, once all legal procedures for vesting these lands are over."
