    "chunk_text": "of Kokkilai and Nayaru lagoons as well as their associated wetlands and bird habitats, there is significant potential for development of eco-hotels. However, at present, eco-hotel facilities are very limited in the Kokkilai and Nayaru areas of the Mullaitivu District and the existing facilities are mainly, small-scale guest houses and basic accommodation facilities, which are insufficient to meet the growing demand for nature and environmental tourism needs. (iii) Yes. The Northern Provincial Tourism Bureau has prepared the 2026-2030 Tourism Development Plan with the support of the Faculty of Postgraduate Studies of the University of Vavuniya and under the leadership of district-level stakeholders, through which the tourism potential, the major tourist attractions, resources,\n\n987 988\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dad\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dbb\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0dcf \u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0d9a\u0dbb\u0db1\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2026 \u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dd2 00\n\nincome generating facilities on the Mullaitivu coastline and the project value is Rs. 80 million. \u2022 Pulipentakal Beach Tourism Development Project in Maritimepattu and the project value is Rs. 53.5million. (iv) Sustainable strategies will be taken to conserve biodiversity, protect the habitats of endemic and migratory birds, preserve beautiful natural landscapes and continue to protect the naturalness of those sensitive ecosystems by developing those areas sustainably through eco-friendly tourism programmes. Furthermore, a provision of Rs. 9.58 million had been provided to the Mullaitivu District Secretary for the development of tourism infrastructure facilities at Kokkilai Puliyamunai Lagoon in the year 2024 and the project has already been completed. In addition, provisions had been made for the following two projects for the year 2025, both of which have been completed now. \u2022 Construction of a resting place with\n\nbathroom facilities at Kokkilai Puliyamunai Lagoon and the project value was Rs. 9.9 million \u2022 Provision of passenger transport boats\n\nfor Kokkilai Puliyamunai Lagoon and the project value was Rs. 9.92 million."
