    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dc2\u0dcf\u0d85\u0dda\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca \u0dad\u0dcf\u0d9c\u0db4\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dad\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0dad\u0db1\u0dca \u0dad\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dd9\u0dcf\u0dab\u0dd2\u0dda\u0d9a\u0db8\u0dca \u0dd9\u0dc5\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bbf\u0baf\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0bb0\u0bbe\u0b9c\u0baa\u0bc1\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0b87\u0bb0\u0bbe\u0b9a\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. Shanakiyan Rajaputhiran Rasamanickam) Hon. Presiding Member, I would like pose the following Question under Standing Order No. 27(2) to the Hon. Minister of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism.\n\nTourism performance is frequently measured by the arrivals, although earnings estimates depend on assumptions about the average stay and the daily\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2 \u0d9c\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\n(4) Will the Government inform for each establishment, its room capacity, the annual turnover, the applicable levy rate, the levy amount due, the amount paid, the outstanding arrear, and numbers of Sri Lankan and foreign employees?\n\nI think the question should be on the number of local employees and employees from other districts rather than foreign employees. If you look at a country like the Maldives, there is a certain percentage of Maldivians that should work in a hotel. In our case also, Hon. Deputy Minister, we should adopt a procedure that star-class hotels employ locals from that area as opposed to employing people from outside the area. At present, star-class hotels employ locals from areas mainly for gardening, cleaning and for other odd jobs. You have to train them at some point to upskill them and bring them up to the required standard.\n\n(5) Before establishing new tourism zones or allocating further State land for hotel development, will the Government introduce enforceable requirements on local employment, local procurement and community benefits and publish annual district-level information on compliance?"
