    "chunk_text": "(iv) the measures that will be taken to encourage private sector investment in the tourism sector in the said district;\n\n(v) whether there is any plan to train and employ the youth of the Mullaitivu District as tour guides, eco-tourism facility providers or professionals in the hospitality sector; and\n\n(b) If not, why?\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab (\u0db8\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dcf\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba) \u0dd4\u0dab\u0dc0\u0dca \u0dc3\u0dab\u0dc3\u0dd2\u0dcf\u0d82\u0dc4\u0dc3 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0dca\u0dcf\u0d82\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0d9a \u0db1\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u200d \u0d85\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad\u200d\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dcf) (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0bb5\u0baa\u0bb0\u0bbe\u0b9a\u0bbf\u0bbe\u0bbf\u0baf\u0bb0\u0bcd) \u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bb5\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0bb0\u0ba3\u0b9a\u0bbf\u0b99\u0bcd\u0bb9 - \u0b9a\u0bc1\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0baa\u0bcd \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf \u0b85\u0b95\u0bae\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0bb0\u0bcd) (The Hon. (Prof.) Ruwan Ranasinghe - Deputy Minister of Tourism) Hon. Speaker, on behalf of the Minister of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism, I answer the Question.\n\n(a) (i) The Government has identified the tourism potential of the tourist attractions in the Northern Province, including in the Mullaitivu District. The Northern Provincial Tourism Bureau has prepared the 2026-2030 Tourism Development Plan for the Northern Province in collaboration with the Faculty of Postgraduate Studies of the University of Vavuniya, and plans to implement the necessary programmes to further develop it and make the Mullaitivu District a more attractive tourism destination for local and foreign tourists.\n\nIt has identified in detail the tourism potential, the major tourist attractions, resources, development opportunities, environmental analysis, gap analysis, strategic interventions, risk mitigation measures et cetera of each district of the Northern Province, including the Mullaitivu District. District-level meetings of government and non-government stakeholders were held throughout the Northern Province in the preparation of this Development Plan. The stakeholders\u2019 meeting for Mullaitivu District was held on 13th November, 2025 at the Mullaitivu District Secretariat, where 76 tourist attractions were identified in the district alone and 10 tourist destinations were selected by the stakeholders, considering their tourism potential and development importance.\n\n1125 1126\n\n[\u0dba\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dbb\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dab\u0dcf \u0dcf\u0dc0\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca\u0daf \u0dc4\u0dd2\u0dcf]\n\n2026 \u0da2\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dd2 23"
  },
