    "chunk_size_bytes": 1658,
    "chunk_text": "It has identified in detail the tourism potential, the major tourist attractions, resources, development opportunities, environmental analysis, gap analysis, strategic interventions, risk mitigation measures et cetera of each district of the Northern Province, including the Mullaitivu District. District-level meetings of government and non-government stakeholders were held throughout the Northern Province in the preparation of this Development Plan. The stakeholders\u2019 meeting for Mullaitivu District was held on 13th November, 2025 at the Mullaitivu District Secretariat, where 76 tourist attractions were identified in the district alone and 10 tourist destinations were selected by the stakeholders, considering their tourism potential and development importance.\n\n1125 1126\n\n[\u0dba\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dbb\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dab\u0dcf \u0dcf\u0dc0\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca\u0daf \u0dc4\u0dd2\u0dcf]\n\n2026 \u0da2\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dd2 23\n\nIn order to promote domestic and foreign tourist arrivals in the Mullaitivu District, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism released funds to the Mullaitivu District Secretary in 2025 for the following projects and those projects were completed in 2025 itself.\n\n\u2022 Construction of a resting place with\n\nbathroom facilities at Kokkilai Puliyamunai Lagoon - Rs. 9.9 million\n\n\u2022 Provision of passenger transport boats\n\nfor Kokkilai Puliyamunai Lagoon - Rs. 9.92 million\n\nFurthermore, a provision of Rs. 9.58 million has been released to the Mullaitivu District Secretary for the development of infrastructure at Kokkilai Puliyamunai Lagoon in the year 2024, and the said project had also been completed.\n\n(iii) The Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Foreign"
