    "chunk_size_bytes": 2099,
    "chunk_text": "Furthermore, a provision of Rs. 9.58 million has been released to the Mullaitivu District Secretary for the development of infrastructure at Kokkilai Puliyamunai Lagoon in the year 2024, and the said project had also been completed.\n\n(iii) The Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Foreign\n\nThose two projects are,\n\ndevelopment of access roads and income generating facilities on the Mullaitivu coastline - Rs. 80 million.\n\nPulipenthakal Beach Tourism Development Project, Maritimepattu - Rs. 53.5 million.\n\n(iv) As per the Tourism Development Plan 2026\n\n-2030, there are significant investment opportunities for private sector investors to the develop tourism business in Mullaitivu District, especially in the coastal areas, and necessary measures are to be taken for that purpose.\n\nSir, since it is lengthy Answer for part (v), I table* it.\n\n* \u0dca\u0dc0\u0dcf\u0d9a\u0db8\u0dca\u0dca\u0dba \u0db8\u0dad \u0dad\u0db6\u0db1 \u0dbd\u0daf \u0db4\u0dd2\u0dc5\u0dd2\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dc3 * \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0baa\u0bc0\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b95\u0bb5\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f \u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b95\u0b9f : * Answer tabled :\n\n(v) Yes. (a) Current Programmes\n\nThe Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority has already established a system to train and employ youths in all provinces of Sri Lanka including Mullaitivu District as tour guides, eco-tourism service providers and professionals in hospitality sector.\n\n(b) Implementation Method\n\nFrom the year 2022, all provincial councils have been delegated the power to identify and select suitable candidates as per the qualifications mentioned in Extraordinary Gazette No. 2140/17, dated 10.09.2019 and the selection procedure approved by the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority. Accordingly, the selection of candidates will be done by the respective provincial councils, considering the needs and demands of the respective province. This programme is implemented covering all nine provinces of Sri Lanka, including the Northern Province and the Mullaitivu District. All the guidelines, procedures, required documents and written instructions required for the implementation of this programme have been communicated to all provincial councils on 25.01.2022."
