    "chunk_size_bytes": 1438,
    "chunk_text": "From the year 2022, all provincial councils have been delegated the power to identify and select suitable candidates as per the qualifications mentioned in Extraordinary Gazette No. 2140/17, dated 10.09.2019 and the selection procedure approved by the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority. Accordingly, the selection of candidates will be done by the respective provincial councils, considering the needs and demands of the respective province. This programme is implemented covering all nine provinces of Sri Lanka, including the Northern Province and the Mullaitivu District. All the guidelines, procedures, required documents and written instructions required for the implementation of this programme have been communicated to all provincial councils on 25.01.2022.\n\nThe selected candidates will be referred to the relevant training programmes conducted by the Sri Lanka Institute of Tourism and Hotel Management and candidates who successfully complete the training and pass the prescribed examinations will be eligible to obtain licences.\n\n(d) Licence Insurance Process\n\nAfter the Sri Lanka Institute of Tourism and Hotel Management forwards the examination results to the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority, the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority issues the relevant licences free of charge upon payment of the prescribed fee by the applicant to the relevant provincial council and submission of the required documents."
  },
