    "md5": "f43b682fa9cf0d69dabcac7a9e1420d6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2000,
    "chunk_text": "2.2 Applications for the registration of birth occurring outside Sri Lanka and citizenship by descent may be submitted through the Deputy High Commission of Sri Lanka in Chennai. The Deputy High Commission\n\n1173 1174\n\n2026 \u0da2\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dd2 23\n\nfacilitates the processing of such applications in coordination with the Registrar General\u2019s Department and the Department of Immigration and Emigration of Sri Lanka.\n\n2.4 The registration of birth and citizenship should, as far as possible, be completed within one year from the date of birth. However, where an application is submitted after the expiry of one year, it may still be processed as a delayed registration subject to the prescribed procedures, payment of the applicable additional fees, submission of the required supporting documents and the completion of the necessary verification process.\n\n2.5 In order to improve access to consular service for Sri Lankan nationals residing in the State of Tamil Nadu,, including those residing in refugee or rehabilitation camps, the Deputy High Commission of Sri Lanka in Chennai may, from time to time, organize consular mobile service programmes in accordance with the consular mobile service guidelines issued by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism. These mobile services facilitate inter alia the registration of births and applications for citizenship by descent. The organization of such programmes is subject to the identification of suitable locations, assessment of public demand, availability of the required logistical arrangements and the prior approval of the Ministry.\n\n3. Voluntary repatriation, livelihood assistance and resettlement.\n\n3.1 The Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism does not administer financial allocations or programmes relating to land allocation, housing assistance, livelihood development, land restoration or resettlement of persons who voluntarily return to Sri Lanka whether from Chennai or from any other country."
