    "chunk_text": "Further, by Gazette Extraordinary No. 2135/13 dated 05th August, 2019, the reclaimed land comprising the Colombo Port City was declared, under Section 3 of the Administrative Districts Act, No. 22 of 1955, to form part of the Colombo Administrative District.\n\nAccordingly, the Colombo Port City forms part of the territory of Sri Lanka.\n\n(b) Under the Tripartite Agreement dated 12th August,\n\nThe leasehold interests in those land parcels were granted by the UDA through Master Leases for a period of 99 years, and have been duly registered in the Land Registry. The statutory authority for those lease arrangements is further recognized under the Colombo Port City Economic Commission Act, No. 11 of 2021, which defines \u201cProject Company Marketable Land\u201d in Section 75 as the proportion of the reclaimed land situated\n\nwithin the Area of Authority of the Colombo Port City made available to the Project Company by way of Master Leases issued by the UDA.\n\nSince the execution of the said Master Leases, CHEC Port City Colombo (Private) Limited has surrendered leases over 10 land parcels comprising a total extent of 12.99 hectares. Thereafter, the Colombo Port City Economic Commission executed leases in respect of the same land parcels with investors for the purpose of carrying out the approved developments on those plots.\n\nAccordingly, the balance land presently held under Master Leases by the Project Company continues to constitute \u201cProject Company Marketable Land\u201d, as defined in Section 75 of the Colombo Port City Economic Commission Act and remain subject to the leasehold framework established under the Tripartite Agreement, the relevant Master Leases and the Colombo Port City Economic Commission Act.\n\n(c) Persons or entities who obtain land within the Colombo Port City do not acquire freehold ownership of land."
