    "chunk_text": "Accordingly, the balance land presently held under Master Leases by the Project Company continues to constitute \u201cProject Company Marketable Land\u201d, as defined in Section 75 of the Colombo Port City Economic Commission Act and remain subject to the leasehold framework established under the Tripartite Agreement, the relevant Master Leases and the Colombo Port City Economic Commission Act.\n\n(c) Persons or entities who obtain land within the Colombo Port City do not acquire freehold ownership of land.\n\nThe leases granted thereunder are for a period of up to 99 years.\n\n(d) The lessee holds the land on a leasehold basis for a term of up to 99 years. Upon the expiry of the lease term, the lessee is required to yield vacant and peaceful possession of the Development Site together with any buildings, fixtures and fittings remaining thereon to the lessor.\n\nFurther, any portion of the Development Site and any associated leasehold rights that remain vested in the lessee and have not been lawfully transferred in accordance with the Colombo Port City Economic Commission Act and the relevant transaction documents shall be surrendered to and vest in the Colombo Port City Economic Commission in accordance with the terms of the applicable Indenture of Lease.\n\nIt is important to note, however, that while the underlying land within the Area of Authority of the Colombo Port City is made available exclusively on a leasehold basis, the Colombo Port City Economic Commission Act expressly contemplates the creation and disposition of condominium parcels. In terms of Sections 38(c) and 38(d) of the Colombo Port City Economic Commission Act, No. 11 of 2021, the Commission may, jointly with the relevant investor, developer or Project Company, lease or\n\n1181 1182\n\n2026 \u0da2\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dd2 23"
