    "chunk_text": "Upon the natural expiry of the lease, as provided for in the Indenture of Lease, the Development Site is to be handed back to the Colombo Port City Economic Commission and the Commission is not obliged to compensate the lessee for any improvements or developments remaining on the site, and the lessee does not require the removal of buildings upon expiry.\n\nProvision 2.6 (d) of the Indenture of Lease provides as follows:\n\n(g) The Colombo Port City Economic Commission Act already provides mechanisms through which Parliament may be informed of matters relating to the administration of assets within the Port City. In particular, Section 6(1)(aa) requires the Commission to submit an Annual Report on its operations, income and expenditure to be placed before Parliament, while Section 15(2) requires audited financial reports to be tabled in Parliament.\n\nIn addition, Section 6(1)(z) empowers the President or the relevant Minister to require the Commission to submit reports on any specific matter relating to the Colombo Port City. While\n\nthe Act does not expressly require periodic reporting to Parliament on the legal status, ownership structure and future disposition of every State land parcel and asset within the Port City, it establishes statutory reporting mechanisms and a transparent legal framework governing the leasing and transfer of land and condominium parcels within the area of Authority.\n\n(h) The detailed information is given in Annex 01. In summary, the proposed investment committed for five years is US Dollars 2.1 billion. With regard to employment generation, the proposed manpower requirement for Year One is 14,335 and the number of employment opportunities created as of December, 2025 is, 9,871. There are 176 companies under four categories: 03 duty-free shops, 09 primary BSIs, 101 secondary BSIs and 63 Aps under those categories. I table* this particular list as the Annex.\n\n(i) The Colombo Port City presents a unique"
