    "chunk_size_bytes": 1519,
    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0dc3\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb0\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0ba3\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) Hon. Deputy Speaker, I am overjoyed that the Government has accepted a business proposition which was rejected earlier in toto; they seem to be accepting it in real business terms, which I appreciate again.\n\nWhen you have investments coming in from Sri Lankans or whoever it is and when they are ready to invest, if a doubt exists in their minds about the lease, which would be restricted only for 99 years, then the salability of these land plots would be in question. That had been repeatedly asked at three different stages and the Colombo Port City Economic Commission, which is the supreme body, gave three different answers and I would like to see this as the final answer. Then, when it comes to its legality, the Supreme Court's interpretation certainly seems to override the response of the Colombo Port City Economic Commission.\n\nSo, Hon. Minister, I am flagging this particular question entirely from an investor\u2019s perspective because I would like to see investments growing. But, my concern is, there seems to be a contradictory statement in your Answer given to Parliament. So, I would greatly appreciate it if you would kindly have this rechecked because with what is going on now, you could subsequently, in two, three years, have the investment approach completely changed, saying this was not the interpretation of the Supreme Court."
  },
