    "md5": "bc3007bf80363773c02745129887777e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2000,
    "chunk_text": "Island, we want to find out and bring a closure to those cases. So, as the Minister of Justice and National Integration, I am glad that I spoke today, sharing my personal experiences. As a child, I saw when I was in Kalubowila Junction how they came and killed the man who had been mending our shoes for years in a brutal manner. I had seen the people wounded and who were trying to reach the hospital being beaten up by the racist goons. I feel embarrassed because, now, I meet so many of my friends who are living overseas. After the \u201883 riots, they left this country and they are not here. But, they have forgiven us; those people have forgiven us.\n\nHowever, what I would like to say is, we should not make the same mistake again. We have to understand that we were wrong, that what happened in July, 1983 was wrong. That is why this country suffered for well over 30 years. And, believe me, when we fight for well over 30 years, it takes more than one Provincial Council Election and more than enacting laws to build the lost trust. That trust can only be built with compassion, love, brotherhood and believing in unity.\n\nMadam, I will finish off by quoting Psalm 133:1:\n\n\u201cHow good and pleasant it is when God\u2019s people live together in unity!\u201d\n\nThat is why God created us, to be united. Why? Unity among God\u2019s people is seen as something good and pleasant, reflecting God\u2019s desire for His followers to live in peace and mutual support. That is how humans are intended to live and that is exactly what the National People\u2019s Power wants to do. So, today\u2019s Adjournment Motion is about learning from the past and making sure that such an incident does not get repeated. No matter whatever people try - I do not want to engage in petty politics here - we have a bigger job to do and our bigger job is to make sure that those ugly incidents would never happen, that we all would live like one mother\u2019s children.\n\nThank you.\n\n1299 1300\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0daf\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dc0"
  },
