    "chunk_size_bytes": 2146,
    "chunk_text": "\u0db6\u0ddc\u0dc4\u0ddc\u0db8 \u0dc3\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dd2. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dca\u200d\u0dba\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) Hon. Prime Minister, the Floor is yours. You have 15 minutes. - [Interruption.] Hon. Members, would you all be quiet and listen to the Hon. Prime Minister?\n\n[12.12 p.m.]\n\nToday, Sir, the Members of the Opposition have brought in this No-Confidence Motion and in doing so, they need to establish facts and evidence, beyond the brutality and the enormity of the incident, to show that because of what happened, the trust and confidence we have in the Minister of Justice and National Integration have eroded; they need to establish, through evidence and facts, how exactly the Minister of Justice and National Integration is solely responsible for what happened and that his behaviour before, during and after that incident amounts to a breach of trust and confidence. That is what the Members of the Opposition need to establish here. But, so far, what have we heard, Sir? The noise level of the Opposition\u2019s arguments is noteworthy; I think we all can agree that they are very loud. But, noise in and of itself does not establish facts; hate, personal attacks, venom and rhetoric cannot establish facts. What we have heard and what we are hearing today is a high level of noise. Also, what we are hearing in terms of facts is a distortion of truth, misrepresentation of facts, half-truth at best and a deliberate effort to personally and viciously attack a Member of the Cabinet. That does not establish, in any way, the intent of this Motion of No Confidence. So, predictably, the Opposition will, once again, fail in their efforts to embarrass, belittle or, in any way, undermine the confidence in this Government or in any Member of this Cabinet.\n\nSir, let us take what happened into account. Yes, we lost 32 lives: the lives of 10 prison officers and 22 prisoners. That is a fact and that is something that we need to investigate into, hold those responsible\n\n1381 1382\n\n2026 \u0da2\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dd2 2 4"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-07-24-2026-07-24",
    "num": "2026-07-24",
    "date_str": "2026-07-24",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-07-24",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/24106_english_2026-07-24.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-07-24-2026-07-24-0106",
    "chunk_index": 106,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "48d7fcf2189fad2998e6d95eed637e5f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1223,
    "chunk_text": "Sir, let us take what happened into account. Yes, we lost 32 lives: the lives of 10 prison officers and 22 prisoners. That is a fact and that is something that we need to investigate into, hold those responsible\n\n1381 1382\n\n2026 \u0da2\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dd2 2 4\n\nThen, what else has been done? Much has been said about the inadequacies in the Department of Government Analyst. Yes, we agree and we know that. That is why the vacancies in the Department of Government Analyst have been filled; that is why money has been allocated for the purchasing of the much-needed equipment, which had not been purchased until two years ago. The procurement process has started for all of those things, none of which have happened earlier. Also, the procedures and processes in the Department of Government Analyst are being reviewed and revised and interventions have been made to speed up its work. So, that is what the Hon. Minister has been doing for the last two years. And, yes, the Department of Government Analyst is heavily under-resourced and understaffed. But, that did not happen during the last two years. That was the Department of Government Analyst this Government inherited and the Hon. Minister had to take on. Let us not forget that."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-07-24-2026-07-24",
    "num": "2026-07-24",
