    "md5": "5e1954165ec5211cc1a5a0b8ef832b2f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1450,
    "chunk_text": "So, Sir, this is the corrupt system that this Minister of Justice has been tasked with cleaning up, and that involves investigations within the institution itself and transferring, investigation and prosecution of his own officials! Therefore, it is not an easy task, but he has begun that task. This Government has undertaken that extremely difficult challenge of cleaning up within, cleaning up the institutions. We inherited institutions which were destroyed, corrupt and where corruption was the reason for the existence of many of those institutions. We also know of a Deputy Minister of Justice who went into a prison drunk and threatened prisoners just because he could! That was the culture that existed and that is the culture this Minister of Justice is trying to reform, trying to change.\n\nSo, Sir, that is the situation and I do not believe this Opposition is capable of bringing in an argument strong enough to support the Motion they have presented. And, as a Government, we have full trust in our Colleague, the Minister of Justice and National Integration. This is not rhetoric, Sir, but he has demonstrated his integrity, his commitment and his dedication to deliver on the\n\nresponsibility he has been tasked with. I am sure, at the end of the day, that image, the image of this Government and the respect we have for our mandate will only be reinforced and reconfirmed. I thank the Opposition for giving us the opportunity to do so."
  },
