    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/24107_english_2026-08-04.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-08-04-2026-08-04-0085",
    "chunk_index": 85,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "4d8ad297ca96030d94deb7baee89cab2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1827,
    "chunk_text": "(e) With regard to the lands belonging to the Government and civilian residents in the Keppapilavu area of Mullaitivu District, which are currently being utilized by the Sri Lanka Army, only 44 out of the 55 civilian claimants of the respective land parcels expressed their willingness to accept alternative lands in lieu of their original lands, where we have put up a model camp adjoining the same land.\n\nFurthermore, the Divisional Secretariat of Muhudubadapattu was informed to ascertain from the 11 civilians who had not accepted the alternative lands and houses whether they would agree to receive compensation based on the value assessed by the Government for the aforementioned land parcels, which they claim to belong to them, and transfer those lands to the Sri Lanka Army. Accordingly, although the Divisional Secretariat inquired from them in this regard, they did not express their consent.\n\nHowever, the Divisional Secretary of Muhudubadapattu has informed on several occasions that land plots corresponding to the extent of the lands previously claimed by the 11 civilians who did not accept the lands and houses in the Keppapilavu Model Village, could be allocated from the remaining portion of the land occupied by the Sri Lanka Army and that houses could be constructed for them.\n\nSo, as I said, when I went to Mullaitivu last week, I met the District Secretary and then spoke with the people who are demanding those lands and told them, \u201cWe can release the lands after considering all the other concerns.\u201d That is a total of 6.7 acres for those 11 civilians. So, we discussed the matter with the District Secretary also, along with the Governor of the Northern Province. The response from those civilians is yet to come. Once it is received, we are willing to release the lands to the District Secretary."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-08-04-2026-08-04",
