    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/24107_english_2026-08-04.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-08-04-2026-08-04-0086",
    "chunk_index": 86,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "8371e13f9cf7aa8091267d798da794c3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1763,
    "chunk_text": "So, as I said, when I went to Mullaitivu last week, I met the District Secretary and then spoke with the people who are demanding those lands and told them, \u201cWe can release the lands after considering all the other concerns.\u201d That is a total of 6.7 acres for those 11 civilians. So, we discussed the matter with the District Secretary also, along with the Governor of the Northern Province. The response from those civilians is yet to come. Once it is received, we are willing to release the lands to the District Secretary.\n\nThank you, Sir.\n\n\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc2\u0dcf\u0dab\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca \u0dbb\u0dcf\u0da2\u0db4\u0dd4\u0dad\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0db1\u0dca \u0dbb\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0dca\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dab\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0dca\u0d9a\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bbf\u0baf\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0bb0\u0bbe\u0b9c\u0baa\u0bc1\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0b87\u0bb0\u0bbe\u0b9a\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. Shanakiyan Rajaputhiran Rasamanickam) Thank you, Hon. Deputy Minister. I would like to contradict a few things in your Statement. You said that these lands are not occupied by the military, but in reality, they are occupied by the military. Most of these lands are civilian lands and they have not been released yet. So, in that sense, they are occupied.\n\nAt the same time, you mentioned that some of these camps are essential for preventing trafficking of narcotics, people smuggling and for other reasons. Then, I would like to ask you why you do not have the same number of camps on the western coast and the southern coast because narcotics are being smuggled not only from the North and the East, Hon. Deputy Minister. So, please do not bring up containing narcotics as an excuse.\n\nAlso, I have always said that I thank you for releasing some of the land used for camps in Batticaloa; we are very thankful to you for releasing them."
  },
